# Cloudflare Pages doesn't know about React Router's client-side routes
# (/admin/dashboard, /admin/masters, etc.) — without this, refreshing or
# directly visiting any route other than "/" 404s, because Cloudflare looks
# for a literal file/folder at that path and finds none. This sends every
# path that isn't a real static asset to index.html instead, and lets
# React Router take over from there.
/*    /index.html   200
